		{
			"id": "111383918073720249",
			"parentId": "111383513691411458",
			"url": "https://techhub.social/@develwithoutacause/111383918022315878",
			"author": {
				"name": "Doug Parker 🕸️",
				"url": "https://techhub.social/@develwithoutacause",
				"avatarUrl": "https://cdn.masto.host/fediversezachleatcom/cache/accounts/avatars/109/332/518/937/677/894/original/e1e878ed6a905b12.jpg"
			},
			"date": "2023-11-10T02:35:10.000Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://front-end.social/@chriscoyier\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>chriscoyier</span></a></span> <span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>zachleat</span></a></span> I'm curious to hear what you both think are the common \"default\" problems Shadow DOM fails to solve?</p><p>Are there any specific shortcomings where you think there are better alternatives?</p>",
			"via": "fediverse"
		},
		{
			"id": "111384016407886999",
			"parentId": "111383918073720249",
			"url": "https://front-end.social/@chriscoyier/111384016119647621",
			"author": {
				"name": "Chris Coyier",
				"url": "https://front-end.social/@chriscoyier",
				"avatarUrl": "https://cdn.masto.host/fediversezachleatcom/cache/accounts/avatars/109/304/727/940/072/717/original/3ab3da2cd9d6bdda.jpg"
			},
			"date": "2023-11-10T03:00:06.000Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://techhub.social/@develwithoutacause\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>develwithoutacause</span></a></span> <span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>zachleat</span></a></span> It's styling for me. ::part and custom properties sneaking through are not real styling solutions. Plopping a chunk of CSS into a template literal I think is clunky and weird. Adopted stylesheets are another request and also weird. So just screw it. Light DOM. I want to use my regular CSS to style things. *generally*.</p>",
			"via": "fediverse"
		},
		{
			"id": "111384227259073455",
			"parentId": "111383176792146470",
			"url": "https://mastodon.social/@ollicle/111384227229043389",
			"private": true,
			"date": "2023-11-10T03:53:48.000Z",
			"via": "fediverse"
		},
		{
			"id": "111384700596604076",
			"parentId": "111383513691411458",
			"url": "https://mastodon.social/@xro/111384700563701836",
			"author": {
				"name": "Raphael",
				"url": "https://mastodon.social/@xro",
				"avatarUrl": "https://cdn.masto.host/fediversezachleatcom/cache/accounts/avatars/109/301/140/932/964/665/original/44eb3ac301f13a36.jpeg"
			},
			"date": "2023-11-10T05:54:10.000Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://front-end.social/@chriscoyier\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>chriscoyier</span></a></span> <span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>zachleat</span></a></span> <br>I think context is important here regarding defaults. For my personal components I‘d rarely use Shadow DOM, but for a lib with a lot of uncertaint usage scenarios and distribution on a per-component basis, Shadow DOM seems like a reasonable default in a lot of cases.</p>",
			"via": "fediverse"
		},
		{
			"id": "111384988232526720",
			"parentId": "111384016407886999",
			"url": "https://mastodon.social/@jakelazaroff/111384988177631235",
			"author": {
				"name": "jake lazaroff",
				"url": "https://mastodon.social/@jakelazaroff",
				"avatarUrl": "https://cdn.masto.host/fediversezachleatcom/cache/accounts/avatars/109/829/533/556/740/279/original/69a92e79689324bc.png"
			},
			"date": "2023-11-10T07:07:19.000Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://front-end.social/@chriscoyier\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>chriscoyier</span></a></span> i’m also in this camp, but slots are only usable with shadow DOM. <span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://fosstodon.org/@justinfagnani\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>justinfagnani</span></a></span> proposed “open-stylable” shadow roots which seem like the best of both worlds: <a href=\"https://github.com/WICG/webcomponents/issues/909\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" translate=\"no\" target=\"_blank\"><span class=\"invisible\">https://</span><span class=\"ellipsis\">github.com/WICG/webcomponents/</span><span class=\"invisible\">issues/909</span></a></p><p><span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://techhub.social/@develwithoutacause\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>develwithoutacause</span></a></span> <span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>zachleat</span></a></span></p>",
			"via": "fediverse"
		},
		{
			"id": "111385094289961434",
			"parentId": "111384988232526720",
			"url": "https://techhub.social/@develwithoutacause/111385094252600996",
			"author": {
				"name": "Doug Parker 🕸️",
				"url": "https://techhub.social/@develwithoutacause",
				"avatarUrl": "https://cdn.masto.host/fediversezachleatcom/cache/accounts/avatars/109/332/518/937/677/894/original/e1e878ed6a905b12.jpg"
			},
			"date": "2023-11-10T07:34:17.000Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://mastodon.social/@jakelazaroff\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>jakelazaroff</span></a></span> <span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://front-end.social/@chriscoyier\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>chriscoyier</span></a></span> <span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://fosstodon.org/@justinfagnani\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>justinfagnani</span></a></span> <span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>zachleat</span></a></span> I get the need, but I feel like open-styleable is a nuclear option.</p><p>I'm all for improvements to APIs like CSS parts, and I'd rather fix those than throw away style isolation altogether.</p>",
			"via": "fediverse"
		},
		{
