			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>zachleat</span></a></span> <span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://techhub.social/@develwithoutacause\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>develwithoutacause</span></a></span> <span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://mastodon.social/@jakelazaroff\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>jakelazaroff</span></a></span> <span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://front-end.social/@chriscoyier\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>chriscoyier</span></a></span> <span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://fosstodon.org/@justinfagnani\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>justinfagnani</span></a></span> </p><p>It makes no sense to me to use slots without shadow DOM.<br>How do you envision this being used and how it would work?</p><p>I mean, if you're \"just\" cloning a template to replace the initial light DOM, it's 10 lines to `querySelector` the initial children and move them to the cloned template &amp; replace children.<br>→ <a href=\"https://codepen.io/tbroyer/details/vYbmbXx\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" translate=\"no\" target=\"_blank\"><span class=\"invisible\">https://</span><span class=\"ellipsis\">codepen.io/tbroyer/details/vYb</span><span class=\"invisible\">mbXx</span></a></p><p>But that's not really \"slotting\" for me: you lose dynamic manipulation of slots/slottables.</p>",
			"via": "fediverse"
		},
