		{
			"id": "111389152397818788",
			"parentId": "111388347843896928",
			"url": "https://mastodon.social/@jakelazaroff/111389152276905881",
			"author": {
				"name": "jake lazaroff",
				"url": "https://mastodon.social/@jakelazaroff",
				"avatarUrl": "https://cdn.masto.host/fediversezachleatcom/cache/accounts/avatars/109/829/533/556/740/279/original/69a92e79689324bc.png"
			},
			"date": "2023-11-11T00:46:18.000Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://piaille.fr/@tbroyer\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>tbroyer</span></a></span> haven’t been at a computer all day so can’t inspect the resulting DOM tree in your pen, but i think i’m describing what you seem to be doing. tbh i’m not really opinionated about the implementation; i just think this particular cow path is extremely well traveled, so we should pave it. it’s nice that it can be done in userland but imo the platform should provide a solution too.</p><p><span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>zachleat</span></a></span> <span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://techhub.social/@develwithoutacause\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>develwithoutacause</span></a></span> <span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://front-end.social/@chriscoyier\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>chriscoyier</span></a></span> <span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://fosstodon.org/@justinfagnani\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>justinfagnani</span></a></span></p>",
			"via": "fediverse"
		},
		{
			"id": "111390018306706684",
			"parentId": "111389152397818788",
			"url": "https://fosstodon.org/@justinfagnani/111390018278059420",
			"author": {
				"name": "Justin Fagnani",
				"url": "https://fosstodon.org/@justinfagnani",
				"avatarUrl": "https://cdn.masto.host/fediversezachleatcom/cache/accounts/avatars/109/306/676/088/719/526/original/1402f1c70ff2119d.jpg"
			},
			"date": "2023-11-11T04:26:32.000Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://mastodon.social/@jakelazaroff\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>jakelazaroff</span></a></span> <span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://piaille.fr/@tbroyer\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>tbroyer</span></a></span> <span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>zachleat</span></a></span> <span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://techhub.social/@develwithoutacause\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>develwithoutacause</span></a></span> <span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://front-end.social/@chriscoyier\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>chriscoyier</span></a></span> light DOM slots just aren't really possible.</p><p>Any proposal would have to describe the assignment algorithm: what nodes are slotted where. I haven't seen anyone do this, because... there's no way to tell what element any slot actually belongs too, so what elements are potentially slottable, and then how to avoid circularity issues.</p><p>Shadow DOM solves this with two trees, and I think two trees are just necessary.</p>",
			"via": "fediverse"
		},
		{
			"id": "111390027269094353",
			"parentId": "111390018306706684",
			"url": "https://fosstodon.org/@justinfagnani/111390027242623966",
			"author": {
				"name": "Justin Fagnani",
				"url": "https://fosstodon.org/@justinfagnani",
				"avatarUrl": "https://cdn.masto.host/fediversezachleatcom/cache/accounts/avatars/109/306/676/088/719/526/original/1402f1c70ff2119d.jpg"
			},
			"date": "2023-11-11T04:28:49.000Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://mastodon.social/@jakelazaroff\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>jakelazaroff</span></a></span> <span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://piaille.fr/@tbroyer\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>tbroyer</span></a></span> <span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>zachleat</span></a></span> <span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://techhub.social/@develwithoutacause\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>develwithoutacause</span></a></span> <span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://front-end.social/@chriscoyier\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>chriscoyier</span></a></span> this is why I think the solution to a few shadow DOM problems is to decouple the encapsulation features, because slots are the most fundamental thing that SD does, and you can't get interoperable composition other ways.</p>",
